A||N||3||Ozzy||Irritating virus for Outlook express users!||||8||
Z||000000||Ozzy||06-23-2000||02:05 AM||||Hey Gang.<P>Recently I came to discover a virus on my laptop. Not a severe one like the recent 'love' virus but definately annoying. It effects only Outlook Express according to Symantecs' website info. I obviously use this e-mail client. Norton picks it up as "Wscript.kakworm". A buddy of mine had it identified as "VBS_KAKWORM.A-M" by their industrial strength virus protection application.<P>It is a worm virus that enters thru a security breach in Outlook Express. The user only needs to read the infected e-mail to fire up the virus. It then automatically attaches itself to your outgoing e-mail. Symptoms are on boot up. My Toshiba laptop show a blank window breifly displaying "Driver Memory Error" and then dissapears. Causes really slow startup too. It also adds an item to the startup config utility; "CaGou" and adds a document called 'kak.htm' to your startup folder.<P>The reason I'm posting this is because I have e-mailed a few of you in recent times. You will only be effected if you use Outlook Express. If I caused you a problem, please accept my appologies; I had no clue...I just thought my Laptop was glitching on me. Let me know and I can tell you how to get rid of this thing. <P>Good thing this is not a really invasive virus. I would feel terrible if I sent that onto someone. My PC is like another organ to me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>Ozzy||||reg||8
Z||000001||Oreif||06-23-2000||02:26 AM||||Go to Microsoft's website and upload the security update for Outlook. The security hole will be fixed and if you get another E-mail it will display a warning message and give you the option to delete.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ozzy||06-23-2000||03:25 AM||||Thnx Orief...I've been meaning to do just that but have not done it yet. I had them all then downloaded the IE 5.5 beta. Guess they didn't include the patch in Outlook.<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||06-23-2000||11:38 AM||||I changed my profile (?) or something so that my emails don't open unless I double click on them.  If I get something from someone I don't know, I just delete it automatically without opening it up.  I know that wouldn't necessarily help with this one, but at least it's a start.  I'm getting just about tired of all of these new virusi (viruseses?  viri???). <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||1
